      "extract": "[]{#sec:intro label=\"sec:intro\"} The finite logarithm was introduced by Kontsevich (under the name \"The $1\\frac{1}{2}$ logarithm\") in [@Kon99]. The finite logarithm is the case $n=1$ of the $n$-th polylogarithm $\\operatorname{li}_n\\in \\mathbb{Z}/p[z]$ defined by $\\operatorname{li}_n(z)= \\sum_{k=1}^{p-1} z^k/k^n$. In loc. cit. Kontsevich proved that the finite logarithm satisfies a 4-term functional equation, known",
      "extractCut": true
    },
